WEBVTT

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.794
Previously on Supernatural

00:00:07.829 --> 00:00:08.837
Sammy.

00:00:09.296 --> 00:00:11.173
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can.

00:00:11.208 --> 00:00:12.055
Go!

00:00:14.885 --> 00:00:17.095
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:19.406
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:22.476 --> 00:00:23.650
This is dad's book.

00:00:23.685 --> 00:00:25.771
I think dad wants us to
pick up where he left off.

00:00:25.806 --> 00:00:27.814
You know, saving people. Hunting things.

00:00:27.849 --> 00:00:29.399
The family business.

00:00:29.566 --> 00:00:30.866
I got to find dad.

00:00:30.901 --> 00:00:33.153
That's the only thing I can think about.

00:02:01.341 --> 00:02:02.724
I know you're just doing your job

00:02:02.759 --> 00:02:05.073
But the police have
been here a week already.

00:02:05.108 --> 00:02:07.353
I don't see why we have
to go through this again.

00:02:07.388 --> 00:02:10.350
The more he tells the story
the more he believes it's true.

00:02:10.385 --> 00:02:11.809
Mrs. McKay.

00:02:13.597 --> 00:02:15.403
We know you spoke with
the local authorities.

00:02:15.538 --> 00:02:19.337
But this seems like a matter
for the State Police. So...

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:22.003
Don't worry about how
crazy it sounds Evan.

00:02:22.038 --> 00:02:24.130
You just tell us what you saw.

00:02:24.165 --> 00:02:26.295
I was up late...

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:28.391
Watching TV.

00:02:28.426 --> 00:02:30.178
When I heard this...

00:02:30.213 --> 00:02:31.978
Weird noise.

00:02:32.013 --> 00:02:35.078
What did it sound like?

00:02:35.113 --> 00:02:38.144
It sounded like a monster.

00:02:39.604 --> 00:02:42.815
Tell the officers what
you were watching on TV.

00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:44.525
Um...

00:02:45.067 --> 00:02:48.035
Godzilla versus Mothra.

00:02:48.070 --> 00:02:50.093
That's my favorite Godzilla movie.

00:02:50.128 --> 00:02:52.081
So much better than the original?

00:02:52.116 --> 00:02:52.900
Totally.

00:02:52.935 --> 00:02:55.298
Yeah, he likes the remake.

00:02:55.488 --> 00:02:56.794
Yuck.

00:02:56.829 --> 00:02:58.513
That's what I mean.

00:03:00.917 --> 00:03:02.133
Evan?

00:03:02.559 --> 00:03:04.879
Did you see what this thing was?

00:03:04.914 --> 00:03:07.253
No, but I saw it grab Mr. Jenkins.

00:03:07.288 --> 00:03:09.592
It pulled him underneath the car.

00:03:09.993 --> 00:03:11.204
Then what?

00:03:13.131 --> 00:03:15.354
It took him away.

00:03:15.389 --> 00:03:18.621
I heard the monster leaving.

00:03:18.656 --> 00:03:21.527
It made this really scary sound.

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:24.398
What did it sound like, Evan?

00:03:24.956 --> 00:03:29.111
Like this whining growl.

00:03:32.016 --> 00:03:33.449
Thanks for your time.

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:40.331
So the local police
have novel out foul play.

00:03:40.966 --> 00:03:42.798
Apparently there were signs of struggle.

00:03:43.572 --> 00:03:45.461
You know, they could be right.
Could just be a kidnapping.

00:03:46.196 --> 00:03:48.246
Maybe this isn't our kind of gig.

00:03:48.281 --> 00:03:49.765
Yeah, maybe not.

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:51.214
Except for this.

00:03:51.249 --> 00:03:53.425
Dad marked the area, Dean.

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:56.129
Possible hunting grounds
of a phantom attacker.

00:03:56.164 --> 00:03:57.971
Why would he even do that?

00:03:58.006 --> 00:04:02.260
Well, he found a lot of local folk law
about a dog figure that comes out at night,

00:04:02.295 --> 00:04:04.888
Grabs people then vanishes.

00:04:04.923 --> 00:04:06.521
He found this too.

00:04:06.556 --> 00:04:11.687
This county has more missing persons per
capital than anywhere else in the state.

00:04:12.104 --> 00:04:13.078
It is weird.

00:04:13.563 --> 00:04:14.450
Yeah.

00:04:14.523 --> 00:04:17.491
Don't phantom attackers usually
snatch people from their beds?

00:04:17.526 --> 00:04:19.044
Jenkins was taken from a parking lot.

00:04:19.079 --> 00:04:20.563
Well, there are all kinds, you know.

00:04:20.564 --> 00:04:24.908
Spring Hill Jack, Spanworm Gases,
they take people anywhere, anytime.

00:04:24.943 --> 00:04:27.077
Look, Dean. I don't know if
this is our kind of gig either...

00:04:27.112 --> 00:04:30.163
Yeah, you're right. We should
ask around more tomorrow.

00:04:30.198 --> 00:04:31.623
Right.

00:04:32.666 --> 00:04:35.043
I saw a motel about five miles back.

00:04:35.078 --> 00:04:36.593
Whoa, whoa, easy.

00:04:36.628 --> 00:04:38.547
Let's have another round?

00:04:38.713 --> 00:04:40.138
We should get an early start.

00:04:40.173 --> 00:04:43.343
Now, you really know how to
have fun, don't you Grandma?

00:04:45.261 --> 00:04:46.375
You're right.

00:04:47.463 --> 00:04:49.444
I'll meet you outside.
I'm gonna take a leak.

00:06:37.222 --> 00:06:38.605
Hey, hey.

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:41.519
Have you guys been outside? Around
here like the last hour or so?

00:06:42.936 --> 00:06:44.104
Sam?

00:06:46.815 --> 00:06:48.176
Sammy!

00:07:07.503 --> 00:07:09.088
Sam...

00:07:20.766 --> 00:07:23.811
So, what can we do for
you Officer Washington?

00:07:23.846 --> 00:07:25.736
I'm working a missing persons.

00:07:25.771 --> 00:07:28.899
I didn't know the Jenkins case was
being covered by the State Police?

00:07:28.934 --> 00:07:31.318
Uh, no, no. It's someone else.

00:07:31.353 --> 00:07:33.035
Actually it's my cousin.

00:07:33.070 --> 00:07:36.198
We were having a few laughs at
this bar down by the highway.

00:07:36.233 --> 00:07:38.081
And I haven't seen him since.

00:07:38.460 --> 00:07:41.060
Did your cousin have a drinking problem?

00:07:41.095 --> 00:07:43.661
Sam? Two beers and he's doing Karaoke.

00:07:43.903 --> 00:07:46.833
No, he wasn't drunk. He was taken.

00:07:48.794 --> 00:07:50.712
All right. What's his name?

00:07:50.747 --> 00:07:52.214
Winchester.

00:07:53.465 --> 00:07:54.966
Sam Winchester.

00:07:55.508 --> 00:07:56.694
Like the riffle?

00:07:56.920 --> 00:07:58.387
Like the riffle.

00:07:58.512 --> 00:08:00.103
Winchester, Sam

00:08:05.018 --> 00:08:06.985
Samuel Winchester.

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:12.651
So you know that his brother
Dean Winchester died in St. Louis.

00:08:12.818 --> 00:08:15.654
And it was excepted a murder.

00:08:16.251 --> 00:08:17.906
Yeah, Dean.

00:08:18.508 --> 00:08:20.701
Kind of the black sheep of the family.

00:08:20.736 --> 00:08:22.232
Handsome though.

00:08:27.259 --> 00:08:29.042
Well, he's not showing up
at any current field reports.

00:08:29.077 --> 00:08:31.155
I already have a lead.

00:08:31.816 --> 00:08:34.047
I saw surveillance
camera above the highway.

00:08:34.082 --> 00:08:35.582
County traffic cam.

00:08:35.617 --> 00:08:36.774
Right, yeah.

00:08:36.809 --> 00:08:38.427
I'm thinking the camera
picked up whatever took him.

00:08:38.462 --> 00:08:40.470
Oh, whoever.

00:08:42.230 --> 00:08:43.890
Well, I have access to
the traffic cam footage

00:08:43.925 --> 00:08:46.723
Down at the county
works department, but...

00:08:46.758 --> 00:08:49.521
Well... Let me tell
you this the right way.

00:08:49.556 --> 00:08:53.442
Won't you fill out...

00:08:54.178 --> 00:08:55.993
A missing persons report.

00:08:59.102 --> 00:09:00.949
And sit tight over here.

00:09:01.805 --> 00:09:03.243
Officer, look uh...

00:09:04.432 --> 00:09:05.516
He's family.

00:09:06.156 --> 00:09:07.170
And I kind of...

00:09:08.134 --> 00:09:09.131
Look out for the kid.

00:09:10.074 --> 00:09:11.439
You got to let me go with you.

00:09:11.944 --> 00:09:13.411
I'm sorry, I can't do that.

00:09:15.221 --> 00:09:16.729
Well, tell me something.

00:09:16.764 --> 00:09:19.642
Your county has a fair
share of missing persons.

00:09:19.677 --> 00:09:22.478
Any of them come back?

00:09:23.187 --> 00:09:26.816
Sam's my responsibility.
And he's coming back.

00:09:26.851 --> 00:09:29.151
I'm bringing him back.

00:10:15.556 --> 00:10:16.689
Greg.

00:10:16.724 --> 00:10:18.559
I think we've got something.

00:10:19.768 --> 00:10:21.979
These traffic cam take an
image every three seconds.

00:10:22.014 --> 00:10:24.279
It's part of the amber alert program.

00:10:24.314 --> 00:10:28.902
These images were all taken around
the time your cousin Sam disappeared.

00:10:29.653 --> 00:10:31.084
This really isn't what I'm looking for.

00:10:31.119 --> 00:10:31.812
Just wait, wait.

00:10:31.857 --> 00:10:33.038
Next one.

00:10:33.073 --> 00:10:36.201
This one was taken right
after Sam left the bar.

00:10:36.236 --> 00:10:38.996
Look at the back in at that thing.

00:10:39.663 --> 00:10:42.207
Now, look at the plates.

00:10:44.460 --> 00:10:46.427
The plates look new. Probably stolen.

00:10:46.462 --> 00:10:50.716
So, whoever's driving that
rust bucket must be involved.

00:10:57.473 --> 00:10:58.673
Do you hear that engine?

00:10:58.708 --> 00:10:59.939
Yeah.

00:11:00.893 --> 00:11:03.812
Kind of a whining growl, isn't it?

00:11:04.229 --> 00:11:06.148
Sure.

00:11:08.525 --> 00:11:10.486
I'll be damned.

00:11:25.417 --> 00:11:27.294
You're alive?

00:11:28.128 --> 00:11:29.428
Hey, you okay?

00:11:29.463 --> 00:11:32.424
Does it look like I'm doing okay?

00:11:33.552 --> 00:11:34.655
Where are we?

00:11:34.690 --> 00:11:36.220
I don't know.

00:11:36.903 --> 00:11:38.103
Country, I think.

00:11:38.757 --> 00:11:40.328
Smells like the country.

00:11:41.002 --> 00:11:42.518
You're Jenkins, aren't you?

00:11:43.054 --> 00:11:43.977
Yeah.

00:11:45.835 --> 00:11:47.272
Wow, I was looking for you.

00:11:47.603 --> 00:11:48.400
Oh, yeah?

00:11:48.435 --> 00:11:49.197
Yeah.

00:11:49.232 --> 00:11:52.826
Well, no offense. But
this is a piss poor rescue.

00:11:52.861 --> 00:11:56.406
Well, my brother's out there right
now too. He's looking for us. So...

00:11:56.441 --> 00:11:58.551
So, he's not gonna find us.

00:11:58.586 --> 00:12:00.626
We're in the middle of nowhere.

00:12:00.661 --> 00:12:03.580
Waiting for them to come back
and do God knows what to us.

00:12:03.615 --> 00:12:05.339
What are they?

00:12:06.061 --> 00:12:06.775
Have you seen them?

00:12:07.476 --> 00:12:07.702
What are you talking about?

00:12:07.703 --> 00:12:09.586
Whatever grabbed us,
what did they look like?

00:12:09.621 --> 00:12:11.338
See for yourself.

00:12:30.482 --> 00:12:31.615
Leave me alone.

00:12:32.384 --> 00:12:34.278
Don't touch me. Leave me alone!

00:12:51.619 --> 00:12:53.788
I'll be damned.

00:12:56.624 --> 00:12:58.216
They're just people.

00:12:58.251 --> 00:13:01.504
Yeah, what did you expect?

00:13:01.921 --> 00:13:03.568
How often do they feed you?

00:13:03.603 --> 00:13:04.691
Once a day.

00:13:05.008 --> 00:13:08.511
They use that thing over
there to open the cage.

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:11.055
And that's the only time you see them?

00:13:11.090 --> 00:13:13.474
So far. But I'm waiting.

00:13:13.509 --> 00:13:15.410
Waiting for what?

00:13:15.445 --> 00:13:17.276
Their baiting time, man.

00:13:17.311 --> 00:13:19.536
I think that's the least
of your worries right now.

00:13:19.571 --> 00:13:20.303
Oh, yeah?

00:13:20.338 --> 00:13:20.738
Yeah.

00:13:20.773 --> 00:13:22.028
What do you they want then?

00:13:22.685 --> 00:13:24.575
Depends on who they are.

00:13:24.610 --> 00:13:27.613
They're bunch of psycho
hill-Billy red neck if you ask me.

00:13:27.648 --> 00:13:30.366
Looking for love in
all the wrong places.

00:13:44.752 --> 00:13:46.973
Okay, the next traffic cam

00:13:47.008 --> 00:13:50.595
Is fifty miles from here and your
pickup didn't pass that one. So...

00:13:50.630 --> 00:13:52.572
So, it must have pulled up somewhere.

00:13:53.016 --> 00:13:54.480
I don't see any other roads here.

00:13:54.911 --> 00:13:59.020
Well, a lot of these back woods
properties have their own private roads.

00:13:59.523 --> 00:14:00.855
Great.

00:14:13.723 --> 00:14:15.077
So, Gregory.

00:14:15.593 --> 00:14:16.085
Yeah.

00:14:16.887 --> 00:14:18.128
I ran your badge number.

00:14:18.163 --> 00:14:20.860
It's routine when working
A case with State Police

00:14:20.895 --> 00:14:22.752
For county purposes when we have you.

00:14:23.445 --> 00:14:26.589
And they just got back to me...

00:14:30.213 --> 00:14:32.386
Says here your badge was stolen.

00:14:33.172 --> 00:14:36.377
And there's a picture of you.

00:14:41.080 --> 00:14:42.425
I lost some weight.

00:14:42.460 --> 00:14:44.807
And I got that Michael
Jackson skin disease...

00:14:44.842 --> 00:14:45.585
Okay.

00:14:45.620 --> 00:14:47.100
Would you step out of the car please?

00:14:47.135 --> 00:14:48.003
Look, look, look.

00:14:50.053 --> 00:14:52.222
If you want to arrest me that's fine.

00:14:52.257 --> 00:14:54.433
I'll cooperate. I swear.

00:14:54.468 --> 00:14:56.608
But first please...

00:14:56.643 --> 00:14:57.635
Let me find Sam.

00:14:57.670 --> 00:14:59.192
I don't even know who you are.

00:14:59.514 --> 00:15:01.696
Or if this Sam person is missing.

00:15:01.731 --> 00:15:04.067
Look into my eyes and tell
me if I'm lying about this.

00:15:04.102 --> 00:15:07.561
Identity theft. You're
impersonating an officer.

00:15:08.607 --> 00:15:10.273
Here's the thing. When...

00:15:10.564 --> 00:15:12.416
When we were young...

00:15:12.451 --> 00:15:15.458
I pretty much pulled him from a fire.

00:15:16.496 --> 00:15:19.635
And ever since then I
felt responsible for him.

00:15:20.097 --> 00:15:23.628
You know, like it's my
job to keep him safe.

00:15:25.672 --> 00:15:29.968
I'm just afraid if we
don't find him fast.

00:15:30.927 --> 00:15:32.888
Please...

00:15:33.346 --> 00:15:36.308
He's my family.

00:15:37.100 --> 00:15:39.234
I'm sorry.

00:15:39.269 --> 00:15:41.730
You've given me no choice.

00:15:41.765 --> 00:15:44.191
I have to take you in.

00:15:57.897 --> 00:16:00.838
After we find Sam Winchester.

00:16:03.543 --> 00:16:05.072
What's your name again?

00:16:05.107 --> 00:16:06.382
It's Sam.

00:16:06.946 --> 00:16:10.325
Why won't you give it up
Sammy. There's no way out.

00:16:10.360 --> 00:16:11.951
Don't...

00:16:12.535 --> 00:16:14.078
Call me...

00:16:14.113 --> 00:16:15.621
Sammy.

00:16:18.082 --> 00:16:20.460
What is it?

00:16:24.464 --> 00:16:25.805
It's a bracket.

00:16:25.840 --> 00:16:29.594
Well, thank God a bracket.
Now we got them, huh?

00:16:31.888 --> 00:16:34.474
Must have been a short.

00:16:37.226 --> 00:16:40.521
Maybe you knocked something loose.

00:16:43.399 --> 00:16:45.117
I think you should get
back in there Jenkins.

00:16:45.152 --> 00:16:45.711
What?

00:16:46.187 --> 00:16:47.869
This isn't right.

00:16:47.904 --> 00:16:49.885
Do you want to get out of here?

00:16:49.920 --> 00:16:51.831
Yeah, but that was too easy.

00:16:51.866 --> 00:16:54.077
Look, I'm gonna get out of
here. I'm gonna send help. Okay?

00:16:54.112 --> 00:16:54.934
Okay. Don't worry.

00:16:54.969 --> 00:16:55.629
No.

00:16:55.664 --> 00:16:58.456
I'm serious, Jenkins.
This might be a trap.

00:16:58.491 --> 00:17:00.416
Bye, Sammy.

00:17:00.708 --> 00:17:02.627
Jenkins!

00:17:42.416 --> 00:17:44.376
Thank you.

00:19:17.444 --> 00:19:19.195
Okay, officer.

00:19:19.446 --> 00:19:21.021
Look I'm gonna press my luck.

00:19:21.056 --> 00:19:22.976
Your luck is so pressed.

00:19:23.276 --> 00:19:24.909
Right.

00:19:25.201 --> 00:19:27.078
I was wondering...

00:19:27.328 --> 00:19:29.726
Why are you helping me out anyway?

00:19:29.761 --> 00:19:32.125
Why don't you just lock me up?

00:19:33.042 --> 00:19:36.379
My brother Riley
disappeared three years ago.

00:19:36.414 --> 00:19:38.763
A lot like Sam.

00:19:38.798 --> 00:19:40.675
We searched for him but...

00:19:40.710 --> 00:19:42.927
Nothing.

00:19:43.595 --> 00:19:46.514
I know what it's like to
feel responsible for someone.

00:19:46.549 --> 00:19:48.850
And for them...

00:19:51.436 --> 00:19:54.006
Come on, let's keep at it.

00:19:57.567 --> 00:19:59.792
Wait, wait. Pull over here. Pull over.

00:20:11.551 --> 00:20:13.718
It's the first turn
off I've seen so far.

00:20:14.792 --> 00:20:16.544
You stay here, I'll check it out.

00:20:16.579 --> 00:20:17.680
No way.

00:20:17.715 --> 00:20:18.781
Hey...

00:20:19.464 --> 00:20:21.278
You're a civilian.

00:20:21.313 --> 00:20:23.057
And a felon, I think.

00:20:23.092 --> 00:20:25.511
I'm not taking you with me.

00:20:26.037 --> 00:20:27.388
You're not going without me.

00:20:30.624 --> 00:20:32.775
All right. You promise...

00:20:32.810 --> 00:20:36.064
You won't get involved.
You let me handle it.

00:20:36.703 --> 00:20:38.041
Yeah, I promise.

00:20:38.076 --> 00:20:39.984
Shake on it.

00:20:43.911 --> 00:20:45.782
Oh, come on.

00:20:46.532 --> 00:20:48.833
This is ridiculous.

00:20:49.568 --> 00:20:51.612
Katherine, I really think
you're gonna need my help.

00:20:51.647 --> 00:20:54.990
I'll manage. Thank you.

00:20:58.452 --> 00:21:01.372
I got to start carrying paper clips.

00:21:31.985 --> 00:21:33.391
Hello?

00:21:36.615 --> 00:21:38.463
Anybody home?

00:21:53.424 --> 00:21:54.668
Hi.

00:21:56.009 --> 00:21:57.780
How are you?

00:22:03.559 --> 00:22:05.234
Who are you?

00:22:05.269 --> 00:22:09.565
I'm Katherine. I'm a deputy.

00:22:09.600 --> 00:22:11.608
What's your name?

00:22:11.643 --> 00:22:13.242
Missy.

00:22:13.277 --> 00:22:15.737
Missy? That's a pretty name.

00:22:15.772 --> 00:22:18.198
Missy, is your mom home?

00:22:18.233 --> 00:22:20.624
She's dead.

00:22:20.659 --> 00:22:24.496
I'm sorry, what about your dad?

00:22:24.788 --> 00:22:27.082
No?

00:22:28.125 --> 00:22:31.170
Can I come in for a minute?

00:22:31.587 --> 00:22:33.922
I just want you look at a picture.

00:22:33.957 --> 00:22:36.357
Have you seen that guy?

00:22:38.469 --> 00:22:40.825
Look at that picture.

00:22:42.848 --> 00:22:44.356
What?

00:22:44.391 --> 00:22:46.894
That's gonna hurt.

00:22:49.730 --> 00:22:51.363
Missy, sweetheart.

00:22:51.398 --> 00:22:53.901
Go tell your brothers,
I want to see them.

00:22:53.936 --> 00:22:56.487
Yes, daddy.

00:23:13.212 --> 00:23:15.589
Son of a bitch.

00:24:19.226 --> 00:24:21.467
But I've never seen him so angry before.

00:24:21.502 --> 00:24:24.783
Never been followed
by the police before.

00:24:39.830 --> 00:24:42.208
You all right?

00:24:45.252 --> 00:24:48.213
Are you Sam Winchester? Aren't you?

00:24:48.248 --> 00:24:50.003
Yeah.

00:24:50.038 --> 00:24:51.759
You're...

00:24:52.134 --> 00:24:55.471
You're cousin's looking for you.

00:24:56.555 --> 00:24:58.411
Thank God.

00:24:58.446 --> 00:25:00.482
Where is he?

00:25:00.517 --> 00:25:02.519
He uh...

00:25:02.853 --> 00:25:06.065
I cuffed him to my car.

00:25:27.670 --> 00:25:29.421
Sam?

00:25:30.047 --> 00:25:31.382
Are you hurt?

00:25:31.417 --> 00:25:33.133
No.

00:25:33.342 --> 00:25:35.844
Damn, it's good to see you.

00:25:36.595 --> 00:25:39.682
How did you get out of the cuffs?

00:25:39.717 --> 00:25:42.559
I know a trick or two.

00:25:43.560 --> 00:25:45.521
All right.

00:25:45.771 --> 00:25:47.231
Oh.

00:25:47.523 --> 00:25:49.865
These locks they're gonna be a bitch.

00:25:49.900 --> 00:25:53.112
Well, there's some kind of
automatic control. Right there.

00:25:53.347 --> 00:25:55.188
Have you seen them?

00:25:55.223 --> 00:25:56.488
Yeah.

00:25:56.523 --> 00:25:58.734
Dude, they're just people.

00:25:58.769 --> 00:26:00.826
And they jumped you?

00:26:00.861 --> 00:26:04.364
Must be getting a little
rusty there, kiddo.

00:26:04.399 --> 00:26:05.386
What do they want?

00:26:05.421 --> 00:26:06.150
I don't know.

00:26:06.151 --> 00:26:08.010
They let Jenkins go, but...

00:26:08.045 --> 00:26:09.835
That was some sort of trap.

00:26:09.870 --> 00:26:11.947
It doesn't make any sense to me.

00:26:11.982 --> 00:26:13.337
Oh, well that's the point.

00:26:13.372 --> 00:26:14.548
You know with...

00:26:14.583 --> 00:26:18.587
Our usual play mates there's rules,
here's patterns. But with people...

00:26:18.622 --> 00:26:20.429
They're just crazy.

00:26:20.464 --> 00:26:23.008
You see anything else out there?

00:26:23.800 --> 00:26:26.365
He has about a dozen junk cars
out back. Plates from all over.

00:26:26.400 --> 00:26:28.930
So, I'm thinking when they take
someone they take their car too.

00:26:28.965 --> 00:26:33.060
Did you see a black mustang?
Out there about ten years old?

00:26:33.095 --> 00:26:36.605
Yeah, actually I did.

00:26:38.281 --> 00:26:41.284
Your brothers?

00:26:42.494 --> 00:26:44.955
I'm sorry.

00:26:46.247 --> 00:26:49.334
Let's get you guys out of here. Then
we'll take care of those bastards.

00:26:49.369 --> 00:26:51.503
It takes a key, key?

00:26:51.538 --> 00:26:52.844
I don't know.

00:26:52.879 --> 00:26:54.756
All right, I better go find it.

00:26:54.791 --> 00:26:56.424
Hey.

00:26:56.800 --> 00:26:58.718
Be careful.

00:26:58.953 --> 00:27:00.920
Yeah.

00:28:12.325 --> 00:28:14.327
Well, I'll say it again.

00:28:14.362 --> 00:28:16.954
Demons I get.

00:28:17.121 --> 00:28:19.540
People are crazy.

00:29:09.420 --> 00:29:11.026
What the...

00:30:46.986 --> 00:30:49.656
It's okay. I'm not gonna hurt you.

00:30:49.989 --> 00:30:51.699
I know.

00:30:51.908 --> 00:30:53.201
Daddy!

00:30:53.326 --> 00:30:54.661
Daddy!

00:30:54.911 --> 00:30:56.454
Daddy!

00:30:57.080 --> 00:30:58.915
Daddy!

00:31:27.326 --> 00:31:30.413
I'm gonna kick your ass first.

00:31:30.746 --> 00:31:32.665
Then yours.

00:31:44.552 --> 00:31:46.345
Come on.

00:31:46.512 --> 00:31:47.895
Let's hunt.

00:31:47.930 --> 00:31:49.890
Yeah, this one's a fighter.

00:31:49.925 --> 00:31:52.893
Sure be fun to hunt.

00:31:53.561 --> 00:31:55.444
Oh, you got to be kidding me.

00:31:55.479 --> 00:31:57.565
This is what this is about? You...

00:31:57.600 --> 00:32:00.401
You yahoos hunt people?

00:32:01.902 --> 00:32:05.364
You ever killed before?

00:32:05.399 --> 00:32:07.366
What?

00:32:08.659 --> 00:32:11.287
Well, it depends on what you mean.

00:32:11.322 --> 00:32:14.630
I've hunted all my life.

00:32:14.665 --> 00:32:18.377
Just like my father, his before him.

00:32:18.412 --> 00:32:20.504
I've hunted deer...

00:32:20.539 --> 00:32:22.304
And bear...

00:32:22.339 --> 00:32:26.385
I even got a coo-Coo once. Oh boy.

00:32:26.802 --> 00:32:29.597
But the best hunt...

00:32:29.632 --> 00:32:32.099
Is human.

00:32:33.267 --> 00:32:36.068
Oh, there's nothing like it.

00:32:36.103 --> 00:32:40.573
Holding their life in your hands.

00:32:40.608 --> 00:32:45.529
Seeing the fear in their
eyes just before they go dark.

00:32:45.564 --> 00:32:49.450
Makes you feel powerful alive.

00:32:49.685 --> 00:32:52.403
You're a sick puppy.

00:32:53.070 --> 00:32:55.246
We give them a weapon.

00:32:55.281 --> 00:32:58.158
Give him a fighting chance.

00:32:58.393 --> 00:33:00.701
It's kind of like...

00:33:00.736 --> 00:33:03.745
Our tradition passed down

00:33:03.780 --> 00:33:09.001
Father to son, cost
only one or two a year.

00:33:09.036 --> 00:33:14.082
Never enough to bring the lot
down we've never been that sloppy.

00:33:14.117 --> 00:33:16.627
Yeah, well. Don't save yourself short.

00:33:16.662 --> 00:33:19.338
You're plenty of sloppy.

00:33:20.672 --> 00:33:24.635
So what? You're with that pretty cop?

00:33:29.932 --> 00:33:32.935
Are you a cop?

00:33:34.561 --> 00:33:37.112
If I tell you...

00:33:37.147 --> 00:33:41.026
You promise not to make
me into an ash tray?

00:33:45.288 --> 00:33:48.875
Only reason I don't let my
boys take you right here now

00:33:48.910 --> 00:33:52.385
Is that there's
something I need to know.

00:33:52.420 --> 00:33:55.206
Yeah, how about it's not
nice to marry your sister.

00:33:56.077 --> 00:34:01.763
Tell me, any of the cops
go come looking for you?

00:34:01.798 --> 00:34:03.104
Oh, eat me.

00:34:03.139 --> 00:34:06.434
No, no, no. Wait. You actually might.

00:34:08.937 --> 00:34:11.821
You think this is funny?

00:34:11.856 --> 00:34:15.777
You've brought this down on my family.

00:34:17.520 --> 00:34:19.487
All right?

00:34:19.522 --> 00:34:22.546
You want to play games?

00:34:22.581 --> 00:34:25.570
We'll play some games.

00:34:27.864 --> 00:34:32.577
Looks like we're gonna have a
hunt tonight after all, boys.

00:34:32.612 --> 00:34:35.663
And you get to pick the animal.

00:34:35.698 --> 00:34:38.037
The boy or the cop.

00:34:38.072 --> 00:34:40.376
Okay, wait, wait.

00:34:40.960 --> 00:34:43.838
Look, nobody's coming for
me. All right? It's just us.

00:34:43.873 --> 00:34:47.091
You don't choose, I will.

00:34:48.635 --> 00:34:52.055
Oh, you son of a bitch!

00:34:56.726 --> 00:34:59.402
Next time, I'll take an eye.

00:34:59.437 --> 00:35:03.233
All right, all right. The
guy. The guy. Take the guy!

00:35:03.858 --> 00:35:05.617
Lee.

00:35:05.952 --> 00:35:08.412
Go do it.

00:35:08.955 --> 00:35:11.561
Don't let him out though.

00:35:11.596 --> 00:35:14.168
Shoot him in the cage.

00:35:15.294 --> 00:35:17.338
What?

00:35:17.547 --> 00:35:19.323
I thought you said you
were gonna hunt him.

00:35:19.358 --> 00:35:20.589
You're gonna give him a chance!

00:35:20.624 --> 00:35:22.161
Lee!

00:35:22.196 --> 00:35:24.053
When you're done with the boy.

00:35:24.088 --> 00:35:27.014
Shoot the bitch too.

00:35:29.350 --> 00:35:34.814
We're cleaning this mess up before
any more cops come running out here.

00:35:43.614 --> 00:35:45.491
What are you doing?

00:35:53.624 --> 00:35:54.792
Hey!

00:35:56.836 --> 00:35:59.297
You hurt my brother,
I'll kill you. I swear.

00:35:59.332 --> 00:36:01.712
I'll kill you all.

00:36:01.747 --> 00:36:04.093
I will kill you all!

00:36:04.768 --> 00:36:06.645
Lee!

00:36:16.822 --> 00:36:18.490
Damn.

00:36:23.704 --> 00:36:25.372
Lee!

00:36:27.541 --> 00:36:30.210
Jack, you come with me.

00:36:30.245 --> 00:36:31.670
Missy.

00:36:31.879 --> 00:36:34.298
You watch him now.

00:36:43.140 --> 00:36:44.350
Lee?

00:36:44.641 --> 00:36:46.393
Where are you?

00:36:50.439 --> 00:36:51.899
Lee?

00:36:53.976 --> 00:36:56.562
Damn it. Jack, hit the lights.

00:36:57.896 --> 00:37:00.315
They must have pulled the fuses.

00:38:31.857 --> 00:38:33.558
You stupid...

00:38:34.559 --> 00:38:35.810
Hey!

00:39:11.762 --> 00:39:13.723
I'll watch this one. You go ahead.

00:39:18.402 --> 00:39:20.988
Go ahead.

00:39:31.457 --> 00:39:33.883
You hurt my family.

00:39:33.918 --> 00:39:36.441
I'm gonna bleed you bitch.

00:39:36.476 --> 00:39:38.965
You killed my brother.

00:39:39.000 --> 00:39:41.342
Your brother?

00:39:42.552 --> 00:39:44.435
Now I see.

00:39:44.470 --> 00:39:47.056
Just tell me why.

00:39:48.567 --> 00:39:51.310
Because it's fun.

00:40:14.174 --> 00:40:14.988
Where's the girl?

00:40:15.023 --> 00:40:16.391
I locked her in the closet.

00:40:16.426 --> 00:40:18.553
What about the dad?

00:40:20.180 --> 00:40:23.809
Shot. Trying to escape.

00:40:34.444 --> 00:40:37.697
I think the car's at the police station.

00:40:37.864 --> 00:40:41.159
Backup units on route to your location.

00:40:43.745 --> 00:40:45.580
So...

00:40:45.914 --> 00:40:49.209
State Police and the FBI are
gonna be here within the hour.

00:40:49.244 --> 00:40:52.128
They're gonna want to talk to you.

00:40:52.629 --> 00:40:56.925
I suggest that you're
both long gone by then.

00:40:57.092 --> 00:40:58.927
Thanks.

00:41:01.137 --> 00:41:02.910
Hey, listen. I don't
mean to press our luck.

00:41:02.945 --> 00:41:04.683
But we're kind of in
the middle of nowhere.

00:41:04.718 --> 00:41:07.060
You think we could catch a ride?

00:41:07.095 --> 00:41:09.354
Start walking.

00:41:10.438 --> 00:41:12.857
Duck if you see a SWAT car.

00:41:12.892 --> 00:41:15.277
Sounds great to me. Thanks.

00:41:15.986 --> 00:41:17.904
Listen...

00:41:19.639 --> 00:41:22.433
I'm sorry about your brother.

00:41:22.892 --> 00:41:24.894
Thank you.

00:41:26.229 --> 00:41:27.779
It was really hard not
knowing what happened to him.

00:41:27.814 --> 00:41:33.319
I thought it would be easier
once I knew the truth. But...

00:41:34.445 --> 00:41:36.864
It isn't really.

00:41:41.703 --> 00:41:44.330
Anyway you should go.

00:41:57.593 --> 00:42:00.096
Don't ever do that again.

00:42:00.131 --> 00:42:01.270
Do what?

00:42:01.305 --> 00:42:03.266
Go missing like that.

00:42:04.684 --> 00:42:06.978
You were worried about me.

00:42:07.729 --> 00:42:11.399
I'm saying, you vanish like that
again I'm not looking for you.

00:42:11.691 --> 00:42:12.711
Sure you will.

00:42:12.746 --> 00:42:13.468
I'm not.

00:42:14.318 --> 00:42:16.577
So you got saddled on by
a 13 year old girl, huh?

00:42:16.612 --> 00:42:17.598
Oh, shut up!

00:42:17.633 --> 00:42:19.570
Just saying getting rusty there, kiddo.

00:42:20.116 --> 00:42:21.784
Shut up!



